From: Bertrand Marquis <bertrand.marquis@arm.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Apr 2026 19:30:47 +0200
Subject: [RFC PATCH 19/28] virtio-msg: complete transport requests explicitly

Return explicit virtio-msg transport completion status codes across
the request handlers and bus receive path.

Explicit statuses keep virtio-msg core behavior describable before
introducing bridge-specific logic.

The BUS_GET_DEVICES handling now enforces the spec-required 8-entry
alignment contract for offset/count windows and rejects misaligned
queries.

Signed-off-by: Bertrand Marquis <bertrand.marquis@arm.com>
---
 hw/virtio/virtio-msg.c              | 352 +++++++++++++++++++---------
 include/hw/virtio/virtio-msg-prot.h |   1 +
 2 files changed, 236 insertions(+), 117 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/virtio/virtio-msg.c b/hw/virtio/virtio-msg.c
index 6a6b6d59525c..64bd30939534 100644
--- a/hw/virtio/virtio-msg.c
+++ b/hw/virtio/virtio-msg.c
@@ -17,16 +17,28 @@
 #include "hw/virtio/virtio-msg.h"
 #include "migration/qemu-file.h"
 #include "qemu/error-report.h"
-#include "qemu/log.h"
 #include "trace.h"
 
 #define VIRTIO_MSG_VENDOR_ID 0x554D4551 /* 'QEMU' */
+#define VIRTIO_MSG_GET_DEVICES_ALIGN 8
+
+static bool virtio_msg_dev_num_to_slot(VirtIOMSGProxy *s, uint16_t dev_num,
+                                       uint16_t *slot)
+{
+    if (dev_num >= ARRAY_SIZE(s->devs)) {
+        return false;
+    }
+
+    *slot = dev_num;
+    return true;
+}
 
 static bool virtio_msg_bad(VirtIOMSGProxy *s, VirtIOMSG *msg)
 {
     bool drop = false;
     size_t min_size;
     unsigned int n;
+    uint16_t slot;
 
